## Traps

- **SQLite contention**: ExperimentTracker on a single SQLite store fails
  with `disk I/O error` if two processes write concurrently. WAL/SHM
  siblings can wedge the file even after the writers exit; clean with
  `rm -f mlfp04_ex3_dimreduction.db*` (note the wildcard) before retry.
  Always run ex_3 smokes SEQUENTIALLY against the same store.
- **Tracker metric-key regex**: `^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_.\-]*$` — no spaces,
  no parens, no `=`, no `,`. Use the `_slug()` helper introduced in
  02_kernel_pca / 05_comparison whenever per-config dict comprehensions
  feed values from labels containing prose.
- **Tracker non-finite reject**: kailash_ml's `_validate_metric_value`
  rejects NaN/inf with `MetricValueError`. Any computed scalar that can
  return NaN (e.g. Levina-Bickel intrinsic_dim, silhouette on collapsed
  embeddings) MUST go through `float(x) if x == x else 0.0` (or the
  named `_finite()` helper introduced in 04_umap). 05_comparison +
  04_umap carry the guards; ex_2/01 had the same guard from r2.
- **DimReductionEngine.reduce is sync** despite `km.list_engines()`
  reporting `is_async=True`. Same trap as ClusteringEngine in r1+r2.
- **kernel_pca / isomap / lle / nmf-positive-only**: DimReductionEngine
  1.5.1 supports `pca, tsne, umap, nmf` ONLY. Anything outside that set
  raises `ValueError: Unsupported algorithm 'X'. Choose from: ...`. NMF
  also requires non-negative inputs (handled in 05_comparison via
  per-feature shift).
- **DBSCAN/HDBSCAN/hierarchical** still missing engine adapters in
  ClusteringEngine 1.5.1; ex_1/02 + ex_1/03 keep their honest
  no-engine close patterns.
